Current UK search research shows many competing heat-pump journeys are installer-matching or quote-generation services, while decision content focuses on checklists and quote completeness. HQC's differentiator is therefore made explicit in the hero: “Independent quote check — not an installer lead form. We do not sell your details or match you to installers.” The supporting copy now starts with the user's existing quote and the existing free CTA remains primary.

Hypothesis: qualified homeowners may mistake HQC for another lead-generation/comparison form and avoid starting. Making the independence and existing-quote proposition explicit should improve checker-start rate without adding acquisition spend, personal-data collection, installer incentives or regulatory risk.

